<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for the AUv3 container app.

  **No App Sandbox here, on purpose.** The app's one job beyond carrying the
  .appex into registration is putting the user's ROM images where the
  extension can read them: an extension's container
  (~/Library/Containers/<appex id>/Data/Library/Application Support/S-MU2000),
  which is the only place outside its own bundle a sandboxed extension reaches.
  A sandboxed process cannot write into a container that is not its own, so
  this app has to run outside one.

  The .appex keeps its sandbox. That is not negotiable: a macOS app extension
  outside the sandbox never registers, and LaunchServices/pluginkit will not
  pick it up however correct the signature is (doc/auv3.md).

  The JIT entitlement the extension needs (com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit)
  belongs to the extension as well, and stays in packaging/auv3-appex.entitlements.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
</dict>
</plist>
